implementationPlan.description:
JetBrains label, before the VS Code one: two value changes and a JUnit test that pins both.
- moe-jetbrains/src/main/kotlin/com/moe/util/TerminalAgentLauncher.kt, enum AgentProvider: '        GEMINI("Gemini", "gemini"),' -> '        GEMINI("Antigravity", "gemini"),  // the wrappers run Antigravity (agy) for gemini mode' (#208). The command stays gemini: it is the wrapper's -Command/--command value, and PROTECTED_AGENT_COMMANDS derives from these entries.
- moe-jetbrains/src/main/resources/messages/MoeBundle.properties: 'moe.panel.provider.gemini=Gemini' -> 'moe.panel.provider.gemini=Antigravity' (#208). The Agents menu shows this string (MoeToolWindowPanel, moe.panel.provider.${provider.name.lowercase()}).
- moe-jetbrains/src/test/kotlin/com/moe/util/TerminalAgentLauncherTest.kt: directly after the test `AgentProvider maps grok and keeps CUSTOM last`, add exactly:
    @Test
    fun `AgentProvider GEMINI is labelled Antigravity and keeps the gemini command`() {
        val gemini = TerminalAgentLauncher.AgentProvider.GEMINI
        assertEquals(gemini, TerminalAgentLauncher.AgentProvider.fromCommand("gemini"))
        assertEquals("gemini", gemini.command)
        assertEquals("Antigravity", gemini.displayName)
        // The Agents menu shows the bundle string (MoeToolWindowPanel), not displayName.
        val bundle = java.util.Properties()
        javaClass.getResourceAsStream("/messages/MoeBundle.properties")!!.use { bundle.load(it) }
        assertEquals("Antigravity", bundle.getProperty("moe.panel.provider.gemini"))
    }
Use the java.util.Properties FQN, not a new import line, as MoeSettingsDialogTest and BoardReleaseTest load the bundle. Leave moe.settings.agentCommandHint alone (it lists commands and is still right). Leave plugin.xml's marketplace description alone too: it says 'Gemini CLI' but is not in #208, and is reported as a follow-up.

